# 32-bit ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit)

A synthesizable 32-bit Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) written in Verilog and implemented through a complete RTL-to-GDSII ASIC design flow using LibreLane and the Sky130 Process Design Kit (PDK).

---

## Overview

This project implements a 32-bit ALU capable of performing common arithmetic and logical operations used in RISC-V processors. The design was verified through synthesis, physical design, routing, timing analysis, DRC, LVS, and GDSII generation.

This project serves as the first building block toward designing a complete 32-bit RISC-V processor.

---

## Features

- 32-bit datapath
- Synthesizable Verilog RTL
- Combinational design (no clock required)
- Zero flag generation
- ASIC implementation using Sky130
- Complete RTL-to-GDSII flow

---

## Supported Operations

| Control | Operation |
|----------|-----------|
| 0000 | AND |
| 0001 | OR |
| 0010 | ADD |
| 0110 | SUB |
| 0111 | SLT |
| 1100 | NOR |

